.na
.nh
.TH tomocleanup 1 4.10.44 IMOD
.SH NAME
tomocleanup \- Remove or list intermediate files in a tilt series data set
.SH SYNOPSIS
tomocleanup  options  directory ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tomocleanup removes intermediate files from a tilt series data set
directory, similar to the cleanup operation in Etomo(1).  It can also
provide a list of the files without removing them.  Selected kinds of files can
be retained if desired.  If none of the options for keeping files are
given, all large files will be removed except the raw stack and the
latest stage of reconstruction: for single axis, either the "_full"
reconstruction file or the final trimmed reconstruction file; for dual-axis, either the
single-axis reconstructions, or the combined volume, or final trimmed
reconstruction file.
.SH OPTIONS
Tomocleanup uses the PIP package for input (see the manual page
for pip(1)).  Options can be specified either as command line
arguments (with the -) or one per line in a command file
(without the -).  Options can be abbreviated to unique letters; the currently
valid abbreviations for short names are shown in parentheses.
INSERT OPTION TEXT HERE
.TP
.B -StandardInput
Read parameter entries from standard input

.SH FILES
When files are actually removed, the program writes leaves a complete list of
the files removed in a file "cleanedUpFiles".
